+# Operational wiring: tokenizer, jailed executor (gVisor), DP fail‑closed tests, HIL simulator
+
+This patch adds the following deliverables to help you wire/harden production:
+
+- Tokenizer-integrated streaming proxy:
+  - ops/llm_support/streaming/streaming_proxy_tokenized.py
+  - Uses TOKENIZER_URL to compute accurate token counts; periodically charges DP.
+  - FAIL_CLOSED_ON_DP_FAIL controls whether the proxy blocks on DP failures.
+
+- Jailed executor runtime with gVisor:
+  - k8s/jailed/gvisor_runtimeclass.yaml
+  - k8s/jailed/jailed-executor-gvisor-deployment.yaml
+  - Deploy gVisor (runsc) on nodes intended for sandboxed jobs; use runtimeClassName: gvisor.
+
+- DP fail-closed test harness:
+  - ops/dp/mock_dp_service.py (mock DP service with toggle)
+  - ops/tests/dp_failclosed_test.py (script that starts a stream and flips DP state)
+  - Use these in staging to validate fail-closed behavior before production.
+
+- HIL simulation harness (PyBullet):
+  - ops/physical/hil/pybullet_hil_simulator.py
+  - ops/physical/hil/hil_test.py
+  - Useful for hardware-in-the-loop tests and E-STOP verification in a controlled environment.
+
+Integration notes and next steps:
+- Build and push images for streaming_proxy_tokenized and mock DP; update K8s manifests to reference your registry.
+- Deploy tokenizer service (ops/tokenization/tokenizer_service.py) or an equivalent tiktoken-based service and set TOKENIZER_URL.
+- Provision nodes with gVisor (runsc). Follow your cloud provider docs for installing runsc and enabling RuntimeClass support.
+- Run the DP fail-closed test in staging: deploy streaming proxy, mock DP, and verify that mid-stream DP failure causes block and orchestrator notification.
+- Use the HIL simulator in an isolated network to run agentic actuation tests; ensure E-STOP path is independent of model control path (safety controller outside the model).
+
+Security & production cautions:
+- Do not run the HIL simulator or mock DP in production; they are test harnesses for staging and development.
+- gVisor reduces attack surface but is not a complete replacement for additional sandboxing (Firecracker, hardware virtualization) where required.
+- Ensure cosign KMS, OIDC, and multisig flows are fully deployed and audited before enabling auto‑promote for agentic/actuating actions.
+
